CHAPTER VI
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 23
(1) The City Regional Government has the obligation to strengthen community participation in the implementation of women's protection.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be conducted in the form of:
a. prevention;
b. services and referral;
c. development of information data systems;
d. strengthening of service institutions;
e. research and policy advocacy;
f. control, guidance and supervision; and g. financing.
(3) Strengthening of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), may be conducted through:
a. strengthening cooperation; and
b. strengthening institutional capacity for prevention and services from the community, boarding educational institutions, and the business sector.
(4) The business sector has responsibility in the implementation of Women's Protection in accordance with the objectives of Corporate Social and Environmental Responsibility.
- 14 - (5) The form of business sector responsibility as referred to in paragraph (4), shall be conducted as follows: a. financial assistance to service institutions; b. empowerment;
c. capacity building;
d. publication and information media;
e. provision of facilities and infrastructure;
f. establishment of special institutions for prevention and services for violence complaints; and
g. social assistance that is non-binding.

