CHAPTER IX
OBLIGATIONS OF THE CITY REGIONAL GOVERNMENT
Article 30
(1) The obligations of the City Regional Government in the implementation of Women's Protection, are as follows: a. formulate policies and include Women's Protection programs in regional development planning and budgeting;
b. provide complaint services, health, social rehabilitation, legal assistance and enforcement as well as repatriation and social reintegration for women victims;
c. establish shelter services and/or safe houses; d. establish special mechanisms for integrated hospital-based services;
e. establish PPT;
f. establish UPT for Women and Children Protection; g. formulate standard operating procedures and service referral systems;
- 16 -
h. conduct prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women;
i. provide human resources and infrastructure facilities for Women's Protection;
j. increase support and develop women's protection service institutions owned by the City Regional Government and the community;
k. develop victim services based on communities, boarding educational institutions, basic educational institutions, religious institutions, and the business sector;
l. conduct capacity building;
m. conduct coordination and cooperation;
n. conduct empowerment to increase community participation;
o. develop an integrated data and information system for women's protection; p. conduct control, guidance and supervision of the implementation of women's protection administration; and
q. provide awards to the community, community organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, boarding educational institutions, the business sector and other parties.
(2) The planning and budgeting of Women's Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a, shall be the responsibility of Regional Apparatus implementing supporting functions of Government Affairs and the Agency.

